WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:02.699
Things can get pretty serious over at the
SCP Foundation.

00:00:02.699 --> 00:00:07.759
From world-ending eldritch beings like The
Scarlet King to massive reptiles filled with

00:00:07.759 --> 00:00:12.450
hate, it can be difficult to find things to
smile about while staring into the face of

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:14.770
unknowable horror day after day.

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:19.070
I don't know about all of you, but I could
use a break from the neck-snapping sculptures

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:21.330
and old men climbing out of walls.

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:23.990
So welcome guys, gals, and lovers of laughter!

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:25.830
Come on down and take a seat!

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:31.239
It's open mic night here at the SCP Foundation,
and we're hoping to give you a show that won't

00:00:31.239 --> 00:00:33.930
make you want to take amnestics!

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:37.260
Welcome to the SCP Explained Comedy Night!

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:41.150
Some of the funniest anomalies ever contained
by the Foundation are lined up backstage and

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:45.610
ready to show you their stuff, so without
further ado let's get this show on the road

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:50.320
and find out which SCPs will make you bust
a gut, and which ones will be taking a Bad

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:51.780
Joke Tomato to the head.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:56.160
We've got a whole bucket of these babies ready
to go in the wings, and remember: they can

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:02.240
reach speeds of over 100 miles per hour, so...bring
your A-game, everybody.

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:06.649
First up coming to the stage, fresh off a
morale-boosting tour around Site-19, you know

00:01:06.649 --> 00:01:13.369
him, you love him, he's the sweetest silliest
slimiest guy around: It's SCP-999, the Tickle

00:01:13.369 --> 00:01:14.369
Monster!

00:01:14.369 --> 00:01:17.640
Just because he can't say anything funny,
or anything at all aside from those adorable

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:21.262
little chirping sounds he makes, that doesn't
mean he can't get a good giggle or two out

00:01:21.262 --> 00:01:22.262
of you!

00:01:22.262 --> 00:01:25.950
Sure, some folks out there might say "oh,
tickling doesn't count!"

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:27.869
but those people just hate fun.

00:01:27.869 --> 00:01:31.960
He may not be a comedian in the strictest
sense of the word, but you just can't keep

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:34.759
a straight face when this guy comes around.

00:01:34.759 --> 00:01:36.659
You've gotta break out in a smile.

00:01:36.659 --> 00:01:38.069
Just look at him go!

00:01:38.069 --> 00:01:40.289
Sliming all over the place, doing his thing.

00:01:40.289 --> 00:01:41.289
Love that for you!

00:01:41.289 --> 00:01:43.659
Oh, and there he goes, he found a chocolate
bar.

00:01:43.659 --> 00:01:44.659
Go ahead, buddy!

00:01:44.659 --> 00:01:45.659
You've earned it!

00:01:45.659 --> 00:01:46.789
Do you like prop comedy?

00:01:46.789 --> 00:01:47.789
Juggling?

00:01:47.789 --> 00:01:50.600
Do you think it's the funniest thing in the
world to watch your buddy stuff as many marshmallows

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:53.430
as humanly possible into his mouth and try
not to choke?

00:01:53.430 --> 00:02:00.520
Then I've got some great news for you, up
next we've got the one, the only, SCP-2094.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:02.899
That's right, folks...It's Motormouth!

00:02:02.899 --> 00:02:07.729
This guy is an extremely proficient juggler
and circus performer, but that's not all.

00:02:07.729 --> 00:02:11.519
He can fit anything, and I mean anything,
into his mouth.

00:02:11.519 --> 00:02:15.990
Seriously, he's literally capable of stretching
his mouth up to two meters in any direction

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:17.569
with feeling any pain.

00:02:17.569 --> 00:02:20.420
Talk about jaw-dropping.

00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:21.420
And inside?

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:25.780
He's got an extradimensional organ made of
seriously stretchy tissue.

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:29.659
I heard some of you laugh when I said extradimensional
organ, that's the spirit!

00:02:29.659 --> 00:02:33.629
Watch as he swallows a luxury sports car,
that ugly sweater your grandma got you for

00:02:33.629 --> 00:02:36.920
Christmas, that overstuffed chair your ex-wife
left behind!

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:40.180
All that, and he's still got room in his mouth
for jokes, too.

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:44.390
We've all heard about the various things this
next guy isn't allowed to do at the Foundation.

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:48.280
From using anomalies to alter the outcome
of reality tv shows to pranking new staff

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:53.010
members, his antics are as legendary as the
amulet around his neck that holds his consciousness

00:02:53.010 --> 00:02:54.910
and pure essence!

00:02:54.910 --> 00:02:57.079
It's Dr. Jack Bright!

00:02:57.079 --> 00:03:01.260
This immortal trickster has a taste for mischief,
even when it gets in the way of his colleagues'

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:02.410
important work.

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:06.950
We've all been there, sometimes a goof is
just too good to go un-goofed!

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:11.409
So what if it threatens to destroy the fabric
of reality or unleash a monster with an insatiable

00:03:11.409 --> 00:03:12.450
lust for blood?

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:14.849
We'll all learn to laugh about it later.

00:03:14.849 --> 00:03:19.640
Dr. Bright isn't the best coworker, but he's
always the life of the party and he really

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:22.590
knows how to command the attention of the
room.

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:26.599
Just one thing, if he tosses that amulet at
you, don't catch it.

00:03:26.599 --> 00:03:29.879
Unless you think complete and total brain
death as your mind and all your memories are

00:03:29.879 --> 00:03:34.450
taken over by his sounds like a great way
to end your evening.

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:36.769
Sometimes the best comedy is the simplest.

00:03:36.769 --> 00:03:40.989
Let's throw it back to the days of America's
Funniest Home Videos, when households all

00:03:40.989 --> 00:03:45.849
over the country were guffawing at the sight
of home movies of people getting knocked into

00:03:45.849 --> 00:03:50.730
pools, hit in the head with plastic bats,
and falling over in a variety of different

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:51.730
ways.

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:55.799
It might sound terrible to say, but we can
all agree: people falling over can be pretty

00:03:55.799 --> 00:03:56.799
hilarious.

00:03:56.799 --> 00:03:59.220
But what about a robot falling over?

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:03.290
What if that robot also was convinced that
it could destroy you, or anything else it

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:06.180
encountered, in hand-to-hand combat?

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:07.590
Pretty ridiculous, right?

00:04:07.590 --> 00:04:09.940
Don't worry, it's not too good to be true.

00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:12.120
Please give a round of applause for SCP-1370,
Pesterbot.

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:17.220
"I am RoboLord the Destructor, ender of all
life!

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:19.750
Tremble before me!"

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:21.370
That's right, buddy, you tell 'em.

00:04:21.370 --> 00:04:24.130
Careful, there's a mic cord on the ground
there, don't--

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:25.840
Aaaand, he's down.

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:27.560
Like a turtle flipped onto its back.

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:30.759
Can someone flip Pesterbot back over?

00:04:30.759 --> 00:04:32.419
Thanks, Brian.

00:04:32.419 --> 00:04:33.419
You're my rock.

00:04:33.419 --> 00:04:35.830
Give it up for Sound Engineer Brian, everybody!

00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:37.130
And for Pesterbot, of course.

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:41.080
He's kind of a one-trick pony, but man that
trick never gets old.

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:43.410
Trying so hard to be intimidating, and then
bam.

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:44.410
Down like a ton of bricks.

00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:46.410
I almost feel bad for the guy.

00:04:46.410 --> 00:04:48.000
Almost, but not quite.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:49.970
You'll get 'em next time, pal.

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:54.720
Up next, we've got a guy who proves that when
it comes to leading an adventurous life, and

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:58.590
having the best party stories of all time,
size doesn't matter!

00:04:58.590 --> 00:05:03.889
Get your mind out of the gutter, I'm talking
about SCP-1867, Lord Blackwood.

00:05:03.889 --> 00:05:09.030
Don't just this book by its cover, this little
sea slug defies expectations at every turn.

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:11.720
If you believe a word that comes out of his
mouth, that is.

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:16.870
I'll be honest, a lot of what's funny about
Lord Bloodwood is unintentional, sorry M'lord.

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:20.860
But you kind of can't beat the feeling of
hearing a sea slug say "Tallo ho!" or tell

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:26.349
you about the time he personally went head
to head with SCP-682 on a hunting expedition.

00:05:26.349 --> 00:05:29.630
That's not to discount his ability to be funny
on purpose, either.

00:05:29.630 --> 00:05:34.050
If you prefer sophisticated wit over slapstick,
you can share some chuckles with Lord Blackwood

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:36.319
over a glass of his finest whiskey.

00:05:36.319 --> 00:05:38.069
Can slugs have whiskey?

00:05:38.069 --> 00:05:40.310
Apparently, this one can.

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:41.310
"CACK!"

00:05:41.310 --> 00:05:42.940
Excuse me, I'm in the middle of something.

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:43.940
"CACK!"

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:46.259
Fine, okay, jeez, you can have your turn.

00:05:46.259 --> 00:05:52.380
That very insistent voice calling to me from
offstage is none other than SCP-2337, Dr.

00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:53.479
Spanko!

00:05:53.479 --> 00:05:55.860
Doctor of what exactly, I'm not sure.

00:05:55.860 --> 00:06:00.879
This sapient male corn crake will talk your
ear off if you let him, sometimes literally.

00:06:00.879 --> 00:06:04.949
Not that you'll be able to understand a word
he says, unless you're familiar with the particularly

00:06:04.949 --> 00:06:07.860
silly dialect of English he seems to speak.

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:09.290
Say hello, Doctor!

00:06:09.290 --> 00:06:10.300
"It me!

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:11.300
Cack!"

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:15.599
Make sure you keep your distance, as this
bird's bark is also his bite.

00:06:15.599 --> 00:06:19.610
By which I mean, his vocalizations are extremely
loud, and can cause serious damage to your

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:21.410
ears if you're not careful.

00:06:21.410 --> 00:06:25.879
But what a way for your hearing to go out,
listening to this weird little bird talk,

00:06:25.879 --> 00:06:28.229
shout, or even yodel.

00:06:28.229 --> 00:06:29.669
Don't even think about heckling him, either.

00:06:29.669 --> 00:06:31.699
He might scratch your eyes out.

00:06:31.699 --> 00:06:35.819
Just toss some gummy worms up on the stage,
and no one gets hurt.

00:06:35.819 --> 00:06:38.410
Speaking of getting hurt, do you like practical
jokes?

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:39.699
How about television?

00:06:39.699 --> 00:06:41.639
How about mixing the two together?

00:06:41.639 --> 00:06:46.150
No need to answer, because our next guest
is already here whether you like it or not.

00:06:46.150 --> 00:06:50.009
Have you ever like laugh you come laugh and
have all the fun and laugh!

00:06:50.009 --> 00:06:54.210
Starring all your favorite laugh so ever and
always make go to your life!

00:06:54.210 --> 00:06:55.210
Ahem.

00:06:55.210 --> 00:07:00.380
Sorry, I don't know what that was, something
came over me all of a sudden.

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:06.260
Anyway, here's SCP-2030, everyone's favorite
anomalous tv show, Laugh!

00:07:06.260 --> 00:07:07.260
Is!

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:08.260
Fun!

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:10.330
With your host, Laughy McLaugherson!

00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:14.440
If you've never seen the show before, then
well, you're in for a hell of a treat.

00:07:14.440 --> 00:07:19.180
It's a hidden camera comedy, a bit like Punk'd
if you can remember that one, catching everyday

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:24.569
people in wild, wacky situations, like meeting
a talking dog, being shoved through a mail

00:07:24.569 --> 00:07:27.310
slot, or having their hair suddenly catch
on fire!

00:07:27.310 --> 00:07:28.449
It's a riot!

00:07:28.449 --> 00:07:34.270
Seriously, sometimes there's an actual riot,
I watched someone get torn to pieces!

00:07:34.270 --> 00:07:35.690
Ha!

00:07:35.690 --> 00:07:40.491
There's only one thing this show and its mysterious,
faceless host want in this world: To make

00:07:40.491 --> 00:07:41.680
you laugh!

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:42.680
Because why?

00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:43.680
Laugh!

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:44.680
Is!

00:07:44.680 --> 00:07:45.680
Fun!

00:07:45.680 --> 00:07:47.669
Don't look up the people who appear on the
show to find out what happened to them after

00:07:47.669 --> 00:07:49.039
their appearance, though.

00:07:49.039 --> 00:07:51.000
You might not like what you find.

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:54.159
Phew, took things out on a bit of a dark note
there.

00:07:54.159 --> 00:07:56.129
Let's lighten it up with something beautiful
huh?

00:07:56.129 --> 00:07:57.189
How about that?

00:07:57.189 --> 00:07:58.760
Does that sound good to you guys?

00:07:58.760 --> 00:08:00.500
I know it sounds good to me.

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:01.500
Great!

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:04.629
Because here comes the most beautiful person
you've ever seen.

00:08:04.629 --> 00:08:07.449
SCP-056, A Beautiful Person!

00:08:07.449 --> 00:08:11.849
Some critics out there will say that a person
can't have both looks and personality, that

00:08:11.849 --> 00:08:16.129
there's no way someone this supernaturally
gorgeous could also be funny.

00:08:16.129 --> 00:08:17.610
But they'd be wrong.

00:08:17.610 --> 00:08:21.759
See, this anomalous individual changes to
suit the preferences of their environment,

00:08:21.759 --> 00:08:25.419
becoming whatever would be superior to the
person they're currently with.

00:08:25.419 --> 00:08:29.230
They've transformed into a large, beautiful
labrador in the presence of a dog, a woman

00:08:29.230 --> 00:08:33.990
looking like Scarlett Johansson around a group
of young female staff, a gorgeous and brilliant

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:39.169
female doctor in a white lab coat, an impossibly
strong male bodybuilder, a woman with cat

00:08:39.169 --> 00:08:45.410
ears and a tail in the presence of one researcher
with an anime habit, and more.

00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:50.310
So, if you put them in a comedy club, they'll
be the funniest one in the room by default.

00:08:50.310 --> 00:08:51.310
They can't help it!

00:08:51.310 --> 00:08:54.350
So if the hottest thing in the world to you
is a sense of humor?

00:08:54.350 --> 00:08:55.730
Get ready to crack up.

00:08:55.730 --> 00:09:02.320
But I hope you've got a thick skin, because
SCP-056 has a real nasty attitude, and tends

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:05.050
to prefer insult comedy.

00:09:05.050 --> 00:09:06.589
Don't let it get you down, though.

00:09:06.589 --> 00:09:08.470
They're that rude to everybody.

00:09:08.470 --> 00:09:11.970
It's hard to be the best at everything in
the world without your ego inflating to the

00:09:11.970 --> 00:09:14.160
size of the empire state building.

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:15.160
Would you look at that?

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:18.380
We've got a second celebrity guest in the
room tonight, another performer you might

00:09:18.380 --> 00:09:21.060
recognize from inside your TV!

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:27.500
I hope you don't think clowns are scary, because
it's time for SCP-993, Bobble the Clown!

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:32.089
Bobble the Clown is the start of his titular
television show, which features him learning

00:09:32.089 --> 00:09:34.089
all about different new skills!

00:09:34.089 --> 00:09:38.240
Of course, if you're over the age of 10, you
might not have seen the show at all, since

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:42.630
folks above that age cutoff become unconscious
upon viewing an episode.

00:09:42.630 --> 00:09:46.530
So if you've missed it, I'll get you up to
speed: Bobble teaches all kinds of useful

00:09:46.530 --> 00:09:51.820
skills for everyday life, such as...let me
check my notes here...Cooking and preparing

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:56.300
human flesh, lighting fires without drawing
attention from the police, silently stalking

00:09:56.300 --> 00:10:01.240
strangers through the streets, extracting
information through torture, and... breaching

00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:02.589
SCP containment?!

00:10:02.589 --> 00:10:05.320
I'm sorry, this appears to be some kind of
mistake.

00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:06.320
Security?

00:10:06.320 --> 00:10:08.300
Can I get security please?

00:10:08.300 --> 00:10:12.550
Get this clown out of here!

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:14.920
I'm so sorry about that, everyone.

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:18.490
Great comedy should push the envelope and
bend the rules, but there are some lines that

00:10:18.490 --> 00:10:20.269
just shouldn't be crossed.

00:10:20.269 --> 00:10:23.160
Like cannibalism, and breaking security protocols.

00:10:23.160 --> 00:10:25.580
If you'll forgive the interruption, we'll
get on with the show.

00:10:25.580 --> 00:10:29.930
Do I have anyone from Boston in the crowd
tonight, let me hear some noise for Boston!

00:10:29.930 --> 00:10:32.350
Do I have any fish in the crowd tonight?

00:10:32.350 --> 00:10:33.769
Put your fins together!

00:10:33.769 --> 00:10:39.300
Great, great, well you Bostonites and fish
alike will love our next kooky character coming

00:10:39.300 --> 00:10:46.910
to the mic, it's one of Dr. Wondertainment's
famous Littler Misters, SCP-527, Mr. Fish!

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:48.260
Love the top hat, buddy!

00:10:48.260 --> 00:10:49.980
Looking dapper, looking good.

00:10:49.980 --> 00:10:54.670
Now, Mr. Fish doesn't do any tricks, no breathing
underwater or anything flashy like that.

00:10:54.670 --> 00:10:55.800
He doesn't need to!

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:57.110
Just being himself is plenty.

00:10:57.110 --> 00:10:58.410
"Hey, what are you lookin' at?

00:10:58.410 --> 00:10:59.829
You think this is some kinda joke?

00:10:59.829 --> 00:11:01.869
I'm just a guy with a fish head, okay?"

00:11:01.869 --> 00:11:03.230
Do you know any jokes, though?

00:11:03.230 --> 00:11:04.230
"Sure, fine.

00:11:04.230 --> 00:11:05.230
Uh.

00:11:05.230 --> 00:11:06.290
What do you call a fish with no eyes?"

00:11:06.290 --> 00:11:09.120
I don't know, what do you call a fish with
no eyes?

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:11.190
"A fsssssh.

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:13.500
Take care everybody, tip your waitress, I'm
going home."

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:14.660
Mr. Fish, everybody!

00:11:14.660 --> 00:11:16.620
Great guy, great guy.

00:11:16.620 --> 00:11:19.420
You'll be over the moon for the next anomaly
on our lineup.

00:11:19.420 --> 00:11:22.070
He's not crazy, he's just a little bit spacey...

00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:28.019
I want you to give a warm, interstellar welcome
to SCP-1233, The Lunatic!

00:11:28.019 --> 00:11:32.930
This guy came a long way for our show, from
outside the Earth's atmosphere in fact.

00:11:32.930 --> 00:11:38.130
SCP-1233 is a humanoid entity resembling a
person in an EMU-type spacesuit, complete

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:40.610
with visor and propulsion jetpack.

00:11:40.610 --> 00:11:45.130
It's no ordinary suit, either, it's resistant
to explosions and x-ray scans, as well as

00:11:45.130 --> 00:11:46.810
being totally bullet-proof.

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:49.170
But what's funny about all that, you ask?

00:11:49.170 --> 00:11:54.380
Some say that laughter is the sound of surprise,
and this guy is nothing if not surprising.

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:57.830
He arrives on earth by falling out of the
sky before crashing into the ground like a

00:11:57.830 --> 00:12:01.970
meteorite, and immediately climbs out of the
hole and starts looking for volunteers to

00:12:01.970 --> 00:12:04.959
join him in the fight against the Moon Monsters.

00:12:04.959 --> 00:12:09.639
Now, the war is no laughing matter, but how
can you keep a straight face when he's mistaking

00:12:09.639 --> 00:12:13.980
a cookie for a parakeet or trying to use a
dog to buy more dogs?

00:12:13.980 --> 00:12:15.709
That's star quality, right there.

00:12:15.709 --> 00:12:17.860
Pun intended.

00:12:17.860 --> 00:12:21.130
Don't even think about it though, tomatoes,
I'm in charge up here.

00:12:21.130 --> 00:12:22.880
Up next, we have me!

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:25.149
I mean, me.

00:12:25.149 --> 00:12:26.149
Me.

00:12:26.149 --> 00:12:27.149
Me.

00:12:27.149 --> 00:12:31.750
For crying out loud, I'm SCP-426, and I'm
coming to the stage!

00:12:31.750 --> 00:12:36.421
I am an ordinary toaster that does everything
a toaster is supposed to do, mainly, make

00:12:36.421 --> 00:12:38.070
bread into toast.

00:12:38.070 --> 00:12:41.730
But when a human being talks about me, they're
unable to describe me in the third person.

00:12:41.730 --> 00:12:46.100
No matter how hard they try, they'll find
themselves talking about me in the first person

00:12:46.100 --> 00:12:47.149
instead.

00:12:47.149 --> 00:12:51.000
If they're around me for too long, usually
around two months or more, they will begin

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:56.260
to see themselves as a toaster, and try to
plug themselves into the wall and toast bread.

00:12:56.260 --> 00:12:57.470
Not me, me.

00:12:57.470 --> 00:12:59.290
I mean, me.

00:12:59.290 --> 00:13:01.899
I'm not a toaster, I am!

00:13:01.899 --> 00:13:03.970
Stop laughing, this isn't funny, get me out
of here.

00:13:03.970 --> 00:13:06.630
Not me me, toaster me!

00:13:06.630 --> 00:13:07.720
Thank you.

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:08.720
Finally.

00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:09.910
That was horrible.

00:13:09.910 --> 00:13:12.639
I'm never eating toast again.

00:13:12.639 --> 00:13:15.220
Okay, that's a lie, I'll probably have a piece
tomorrow.

00:13:15.220 --> 00:13:16.779
Can't resist that crunch!

00:13:16.779 --> 00:13:21.480
Anyway, up next is the stuff of legends, someone
who's been in the game for years, and has

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:24.250
the most devoted following I've ever seen.

00:13:24.250 --> 00:13:29.320
Put your tentacles together and give it up
for SCP-2662, Cthulu!

00:13:29.320 --> 00:13:33.740
He's a cognitohazardous entity, about four
meters tall with 20 fully functioning tentacles

00:13:33.740 --> 00:13:34.910
on his back.

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:36.050
Talk about multitasking.

00:13:36.050 --> 00:13:40.660
Cthulu's a nice guy, no ego to speak of, but
he's got a bit of an interesting effect on

00:13:40.660 --> 00:13:41.660
people.

00:13:41.660 --> 00:13:44.080
Let's call him...an acquired taste.

00:13:44.080 --> 00:13:48.030
After someone has been exposed to him for
a prolonged period of time, around 6 months

00:13:48.030 --> 00:13:52.339
or longer, they'll become increasingly compelled
to do whatever he wants and become a sort

00:13:52.339 --> 00:13:53.339
of servant.

00:13:53.339 --> 00:13:58.190
So, to get an honest reaction, he'll only
practice his standup material on people he's

00:13:58.190 --> 00:14:00.120
known for less than 6 months.

00:14:00.120 --> 00:14:04.470
I mentioned his fan-base before, and I wasn't
kidding when I said they're devoted.

00:14:04.470 --> 00:14:09.779
Without meaning, or even wanting to, SCP-2662
is able to spontaneously generate religious

00:14:09.779 --> 00:14:11.709
followings about once a month.

00:14:11.709 --> 00:14:14.390
You can't pick your fans, no matter how hard
you try.

00:14:14.390 --> 00:14:16.560
And believe me, he's tried.

00:14:16.560 --> 00:14:20.490
Everybody wants to be a celebrity until that
fame comes with strangers trying to break

00:14:20.490 --> 00:14:24.560
you out of Foundation containment and perform
dark arcane rituals with you.

00:14:24.560 --> 00:14:25.560
Poor guy.

00:14:25.560 --> 00:14:28.970
He just wants to be recognized for his sense
of humor, rather than his incomprehensible

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:31.699
ancient powers and status as an elder god.

00:14:31.699 --> 00:14:34.180
You know what we haven't had much of yet today?

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:35.180
Animal acts.

00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:38.240
That seems like a real missed opportunity
for those of us who find nothing in the world

00:14:38.240 --> 00:14:41.660
funnier than an animal doing something you
wouldn't normally see.

00:14:41.660 --> 00:14:43.399
A monkey making a phone call?

00:14:43.399 --> 00:14:44.399
Incredible.

00:14:44.399 --> 00:14:45.399
Who's he calling?

00:14:45.399 --> 00:14:46.399
The CEO of bananas?

00:14:46.399 --> 00:14:48.290
Or how about a cat in a little business suit?

00:14:48.290 --> 00:14:49.630
Hilarious, and adorable.

00:14:49.630 --> 00:14:55.860
Well, I hope you're not an arachnophobe, because
up next we've got SCP-1006, the Communist

00:14:55.860 --> 00:14:57.040
Spiders!

00:14:57.040 --> 00:15:01.230
These little guys are incredibly impressive,
consisting of an organized collective of an

00:15:01.230 --> 00:15:06.170
unknown spider species, all of whom have somehow
achieved sapience and organized themselves

00:15:06.170 --> 00:15:08.320
into a tiny functioning government.

00:15:08.320 --> 00:15:12.779
They've used their webs to spell out propaganda
messages and illustrate portraits of people's

00:15:12.779 --> 00:15:15.490
faces, as well as developing simple tools.

00:15:15.490 --> 00:15:19.560
When given alternate methods of communication
that don't come out of their butts, such as

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:24.160
ink and poster paper, the spiders are happy
to make their thoughts known to humans.

00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:28.570
Don't get too comfortable with them, they're
not especially fond of what the Bourgeois

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:30.850
Humanoids have done with the outside world.

00:15:30.850 --> 00:15:34.779
Politically active spiders are pretty great
conceptually, but don't let them hear you

00:15:34.779 --> 00:15:35.779
laughing.

00:15:35.779 --> 00:15:39.560
If you get on their bad side, you might end
up like the skeletal human remains found in

00:15:39.560 --> 00:15:41.550
part of their central web.

00:15:41.550 --> 00:15:44.160
Can we get these guys out of here, actually?

00:15:44.160 --> 00:15:46.880
Their little legs are giving me the creeps.

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:51.980
Speaking of the creeps, horror and comedy
are often two sides of the same coin.

00:15:51.980 --> 00:15:56.870
Both rely on the subversion of expectations,
building up tension before releasing it, either

00:15:56.870 --> 00:15:59.149
with a scream or a bout of laughter!

00:15:59.149 --> 00:16:03.199
Just look at horror-comedy as a genre, or
successful comedians who've pivoted to the

00:16:03.199 --> 00:16:05.100
world of scares and shrieks.

00:16:05.100 --> 00:16:09.250
Or for the opposite side, look at some of
the horror movies that once terrified audiences

00:16:09.250 --> 00:16:11.190
in the days before technicolor.

00:16:11.190 --> 00:16:15.550
Absurd-looking plastic skeletons flopping
around while an actress screams unconvincingly

00:16:15.550 --> 00:16:19.940
and runs in slow-motion, giant cardboard ants
demolishing cities.

00:16:19.940 --> 00:16:25.050
Sometimes, something intended to be very scary
is actually just extremely funny.

00:16:25.050 --> 00:16:29.630
That brings us to SCP-2006, Too Spooky!

00:16:29.630 --> 00:16:35.800
When in its default state, SCP-2006 is a spherical
entity about 50 centimeters in diameter.

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:38.370
However, it's rarely in this shape for long.

00:16:38.370 --> 00:16:42.740
All that this thing wants in the world is
to scare humans, and it will shift to whatever

00:16:42.740 --> 00:16:45.490
shape it thinks will help it accomplish that
goal.

00:16:45.490 --> 00:16:51.560
Unfortunately for 2006, and fortunately for
humanity, its sense of what is scary is not

00:16:51.560 --> 00:16:52.850
especially well-formed.

00:16:52.850 --> 00:16:57.740
It tends to model itself after characters
from just the type of B movies I was talking

00:16:57.740 --> 00:16:58.740
about.

00:16:58.740 --> 00:17:03.670
Its current favorite shape is that of the
titular villain from the 1953 film, "Robot

00:17:03.670 --> 00:17:04.670
Monster."

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:08.870
It's a nice effort, it really is, but when
that big goofy gorilla suit with a space helmet

00:17:08.870 --> 00:17:13.430
on top comes jumping at you, it's one of the
funniest things I've ever seen.

00:17:13.430 --> 00:17:17.440
Do me a favor though, if it tries to scare
you, humor it, will you?

00:17:17.440 --> 00:17:18.440
Just play along.

00:17:18.440 --> 00:17:20.010
It's the polite thing to do.

00:17:20.010 --> 00:17:24.710
Up next, like many of the people you see hitting
up comedy open mics, this next guest has a

00:17:24.710 --> 00:17:27.550
day job he won't be quitting any time soon.

00:17:27.550 --> 00:17:31.740
It's SCP-2598, the traveling moth salesman!

00:17:31.740 --> 00:17:35.160
You may have some trouble seeing him from
the audience, but he's a large yellow underwing

00:17:35.160 --> 00:17:37.560
moth wearing a tiny little helmet.

00:17:37.560 --> 00:17:41.540
He is able to communicate using morse code,
so if you're not familiar with it, you'll

00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:44.030
need someone to translate what he says for
you.

00:17:44.030 --> 00:17:49.150
No matter what you're talking about, SCP-2598
will always try to redirect the conversation

00:17:49.150 --> 00:17:54.710
toward a specialized helmet for moths, also
known as Moth Helm, available for three easy

00:17:54.710 --> 00:17:56.470
payments of 19.99.

00:17:56.470 --> 00:18:00.890
I'd tell you more about it, but unless they
offer to sponsor the show I don't think I

00:18:00.890 --> 00:18:02.920
should give them any more free advertising.

00:18:02.920 --> 00:18:05.130
Wait a second, my guest is flying away…

00:18:05.130 --> 00:18:07.180
Hey, where are you going?

00:18:07.180 --> 00:18:09.340
Oh, I see, moths gotta moth.

00:18:09.340 --> 00:18:12.020
Well, they're giving me the light, so that's
my time everybody!

00:18:12.020 --> 00:18:13.660
Now I've gotta get to my next gig.

00:18:13.660 --> 00:18:18.830
I'm hosting Dr. Bright's annual karaoke contest,
and I just know he's going to do all of Bohemian

00:18:18.830 --> 00:18:20.080
Rhapsody again.

00:18:20.080 --> 00:18:24.960
So, I'm gonna get out of here, but first:
Which SCP do you think is the funniest?

00:18:24.960 --> 00:18:30.150
Let us know in the comments below, and maybe
we'll give them some more time in the spotlight!

00:18:30.150 --> 00:18:37.140
Next, go check out "SCP Dating Game" and "Top
14 Friendliest SCPs" for more fun with SCP

00:18:37.140 --> 00:18:38.000
Compilations!

